# Per-stage config for scripts/run-loop-news.sh — copy this file to
# scripts/run-loop-news.env (gitignored) and uncomment/edit what you want to change.
# run-loop-news.sh auto-sources scripts/run-loop-news.env if it exists.
#
# Precedence (highest wins): CLI flag  >  this file / exported env var  >  built-in default.
# CLI flags (--search-model, --model, etc. — see `run-loop-news.sh --help`) are for a
# one-off run; this file is for a standing local default without exporting anything.

# ── Search stage (Skill A · fetch-loop-news) ──────────────────────────────────
# Model: an alias (sonnet|opus|fable) or a full model id (e.g. claude-sonnet-5).
# LOOP_SEARCH_MODEL=sonnet

# Effort: low | medium | high | xhigh | max.
# LOOP_SEARCH_EFFORT=high

# Max turns for the search session.
# LOOP_SEARCH_MAX_TURNS=100

# --max-budget-usd tripwire (see note below) for the search stage.
# LOOP_SEARCH_BUDGET_USD=30

# ── Integrate stage (Skill B · integrate-loop-news) ───────────────────────────
# LOOP_INTEGRATE_MODEL=sonnet
# LOOP_INTEGRATE_EFFORT=high
# LOOP_INTEGRATE_MAX_TURNS=250
# LOOP_INTEGRATE_BUDGET_USD=20

# ── Note on *_BUDGET_USD under a Claude subscription (Pro/Max) ────────────────
# This is NOT a real dollar cost — you're not billed per token. It's a script-side
# tripwire computed from API list-price-equivalent token usage, meant only to stop a
# genuinely runaway/looping session. Set it generously; it shouldn't trip on a normal
# thorough run. On budget-exceeded the wrapper stops immediately (never retries — the
# same session would just hit the same wall again).

# ── Do not let the scheduled run update Claude Code mid-flight ────────────────
# Recommended, and set locally on this machine since 2026-09-06.
#
# Observed that day: stage A ran 2.1.261, the auto-updater repointed ~/.local/bin/claude
# at 04:17, and stage B ran 2.1.263 — inside a single run the wrapper reported as clean.
# Two harms. Behaviour can differ between stages of what is reported as one run. And a
# macOS per-binary firewall rule (LuLu, Little Snitch) is keyed to the EXECUTABLE PATH, so
# a new version inherits no rule: its outbound calls can be blocked, or held at a prompt
# nobody is awake to answer at 04:17 — a partial network loss indistinguishable from
# "that source had nothing today", which is this repo's defining defect class.
#
# Official: "Set to 1 to disable automatic background updates. Manual 'claude update'
# still works."  https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars
#
# This file is sourced only by run-loop-news.sh, so interactive sessions still auto-update.
# Update deliberately, while you are at the machine, and approve the firewall prompt then.
# The wrapper reports version drift either way (v3.1.5).
#DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1

# Path to the claude CLI. Leave unset and the script resolves it: PATH first, then
# ~/.local/bin, /opt/homebrew/bin, /usr/local/bin. Set it only to pin a specific build
# (e.g. testing a release candidate). An unresolvable binary is a FATAL preflight, exit 3.
#CLAUDE_BIN=/Users/you/.local/bin/claude
